media: rkvdec, hantro: cached decoded frames on request (cache hints)

Khadas Edge1, Android 14 on mainline 6.12. Applied to kernel/mainline by
build/build-kernel.sh before every build (device/khadas/edge/kernel/patches/).

Both decoders allocate their CAPTURE buffers with vb2-dma-contig, coherent, so a
user-space mapping of a decoded frame is write-combined: uncached for reads. The
FFmpeg Codec2 service reads every frame once (V4L2 request hwaccel, then a copy
into the gralloc buffer that goes to the display), and on the RK3399 that read
runs at a few hundred MB/s - a 3840x2160 NV12 frame is 12.4 MB, so card 23 played
4K VP9 from rkvdec at 9 frames per second with the CPUs mostly idle.

vb2 already has the way out: a queue with allow_cache_hints accepts
V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT in VIDIOC_REQBUFS / VIDIOC_CREATE_BUFS (and reports
V4L2_BUF_CAP_SUPPORTS_MMAP_CACHE_HINTS), allocates with dma_alloc_noncontiguous -
through the decoders' IOMMUs here - maps the buffer cached, and does the cache
maintenance itself: clean at QBUF (vb2_dc_prepare), invalidate at DQBUF
(vb2_dc_finish). Neither driver sets the flag, so a request for it was silently
dropped. This sets it on the decoders' CAPTURE queues; nothing changes for a
client that does not ask (FFmpeg asks: patches/external/ffmpeg 0011).

Neither driver touches a decoder CAPTURE buffer from the CPU (no kernel mapping,
DMA_ATTR_NO_KERNEL_MAPPING stays), and the CPU only ever reads them, so the
hardware never sees a dirty line: the reference frames it reads back are clean.

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_drv.c b/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_drv.c
index 137ca13ee..4e3113c31 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/hantro_drv.c
@@ -238,6 +238,8 @@ queue_init(void *priv, struct vb2_queue *src_vq, struct vb2_queue *dst_vq)
 	if (!ctx->is_encoder) {
 		dst_vq->dma_attrs |= DMA_ATTR_NO_KERNEL_MAPPING;
 		dst_vq->max_num_buffers = MAX_POSTPROC_BUFFERS;
+		/* Cached decoded frames on request, as in rkvdec. */
+		dst_vq->allow_cache_hints = 1;
 	}
 
 	dst_vq->type = V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE;
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/rkvdec/rkvdec.c b/drivers/staging/media/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
index a1d941b0b..afe5c903e 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
@@ -756,6 +756,13 @@ static int rkvdec_queue_init(void *priv,
 	dst_vq->mem_ops = &vb2_dma_contig_memops;
 	dst_vq->dma_attrs = DMA_ATTR_ALLOC_SINGLE_PAGES |
 			    DMA_ATTR_NO_KERNEL_MAPPING;
+	/*
+	 * Let user space ask for cached decoded frames
+	 * (V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT): a frame the CPU reads is otherwise
+	 * read from write-combined memory, a few hundred MB/s on this SoC.
+	 * vb2 syncs the cache at QBUF and DQBUF.
+	 */
+	dst_vq->allow_cache_hints = 1;
 	dst_vq->type = V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE;
 	dst_vq->io_modes = VB2_MMAP | VB2_DMABUF;
 	dst_vq->drv_priv = ctx;
